1
00:00:00,010 --> 00:00:11,920
This is Know Your Customer at NEWEAST. A new customer starts as a lead, and ends as a customer master in SAP.

2
00:00:11,970 --> 00:00:23,550
Watch the role on screen. Sales creates. The customer fills. Sales, then the manager, then Finance. SAP is last.

3
00:00:23,600 --> 00:00:33,990
Chapter one. Sales creates the lead and sends the KYC form.

4
00:00:34,040 --> 00:01:12,380
Sales — This is Add New Lead. The salesman is already set. Capture the company.

5
00:01:12,430 --> 00:01:20,700
Sales — Pin the site on the map. The address sits on the map before you save.

6
00:01:20,750 --> 00:01:33,670
Sales — Add the lead. Confirm on the next screen.

7
00:01:33,720 --> 00:01:45,590
Sales — The lead is on Existing Lead. Send the KYC form from here.

8
00:01:45,640 --> 00:01:54,760
Chapter two. The customer opens the KYC form from the link.

9
00:01:54,810 --> 00:02:04,330
Customer — Company profile, bank, and owners. Required fields first.

10
00:02:04,380 --> 00:02:14,240
Customer — Submit. The case returns to Sales.

11
00:02:14,290 --> 00:02:27,830
Chapter three. Sales reviews the KYC, then sends it to the line manager.

12
00:02:27,880 --> 00:02:39,760
Sales — Read the answers. Send to Line Manager.

13
00:02:39,810 --> 00:02:48,550
Chapter four. The sales manager decides. Finance is next.

14
00:02:48,600 --> 00:03:01,330
Sales manager — Open the request.

15
00:03:01,380 --> 00:03:10,320
Chapter five. Finance Lead Approval. People sign in order.

16
00:03:10,370 --> 00:03:32,850
Finance — Open the case. This seat is not last, so escalate is not here.

17
00:03:32,900 --> 00:03:49,050
Finance — Now this is the last seat. Escalate is available.

18
00:03:49,100 --> 00:04:06,660
Chapter six. Escalation. Approve still closes on SAP.

19
00:04:06,710 --> 00:04:13,300
Chapter seven. SAP. The lead becomes the customer master.

20
00:04:13,350 --> 00:04:19,700
Know Your Customer at NEWEAST. Lead. KYC. Approve. SAP.
